<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44023" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sēstos</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-us</span></b> ), i, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σηστός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city in Thrace</i>, <i>on
				the Hellespont</i>, <i>opposite Abydos</i>, <i>the residence of Hero</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Leandri amore pernobilis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mel.
					2, 2, 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 11, 18, § 49</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 32,
			33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">37, 9</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Ov.
				H. 18, 127</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 2, 674</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 55</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sēstĭăcus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Sestos</i>, <i>Sestian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sinus,</span>”
				i.e. <i>the Hellespont</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 1, 3, 27</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pelagus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 10, 287</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sēstus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of Sestos</i>, <i>Sestian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">puella,</span>”
				i.e. <i>Hero</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
				17</span></i>
			 (18), 2 dub. (the first two lines are probably
			spurious).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sē-stĭăs</span></b> ,
				ădis, f., <i>the Sestian</i>, i.e. <i>Hero</i>, <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 6,
				547</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sid. Carm. 11,
		71</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
